# Real config for the PRODUCTION site (Firebase project osf-relay, pipe.jspsych.org).
#
# Firebase loads this file on `firebase deploy` because the project id is
# osf-relay; it is NOT loaded by the emulator, which uses .env.local. Anything
# in this file reaches production. Non-secret values only -- secrets are
# injected at deploy time into functions/.env by
# .github/workflows/firebase-deploy.yml from GitHub repository secrets.
#
# --- Google Drive OAuth2 ---
# The OAuth client lives in the osf-relay GCP project (its own consent screen,
# separate from datapipe-test's). Its authorized redirect URI must be exactly
# the value below: /oauth2/connect is the provider-connect page, distinct from
# /oauth2/callback, which belongs to OSF sign-in. The client SECRET comes from
# the PROD_GDRIVE_CLIENT_SECRET GitHub secret.
#
# GDRIVE_AUTHORIZE_URL / GDRIVE_TOKEN_URL / GDRIVE_API_BASE are intentionally
# unset so the code falls back to the real Google endpoints.
GDRIVE_CLIENT_ID=54492763028-rj9a4uf65oegb40ms806o9vdk4ono4bd.apps.googleusercontent.com
GDRIVE_REDIRECT_URI=https://pipe.jspsych.org/oauth2/connect

# --- Zenodo OAuth2 ---
# ZENODO_ENV is deliberately UNSET here: unset resolves to the real zenodo.org.
# The test site sets "sandbox." and uses a sandbox-registered client; a
# sandbox client_id cannot complete a flow on zenodo.org, so this id and the
# PROD_ZENODO_CLIENT_SECRET GitHub secret come from one registration on
# zenodo.org (confidential client, under the datapipe@jspsych.org account)
# and have to be rotated together. ZENODO_AUTHORIZE_URL / ZENODO_TOKEN_URL /
# ZENODO_API_BASE are intentionally unset so the code derives them from
# ZENODO_ENV, mirroring the GDRIVE_* convention above.
ZENODO_CLIENT_ID=IEgjhEAq42NgnRoYZdM1uwoGLgBQIXefTQKl3MRY
ZENODO_REDIRECT_URI=https://pipe.jspsych.org/oauth2/connect
